# APIx CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub requests review from the code owner when a pull request touches a
# matching path. Ownership here mirrors docs/engineering/ownership-policy.md;
# the two must be changed together.
#
# Later rules win, so the default owner is declared first.
#
# NOTE ON ENFORCEMENT: CODEOWNERS only becomes a *requirement* when branch
# protection on main enables "Require review from Code Owners". Until that is
# configured (see docs/engineering/branch-protection.md), these entries request
# review but do not block a merge.

# ─── Default ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Principal engineering owner is the fallback reviewer for anything unclaimed.
*                               @Rexy-5097

# ─── Statistics and methodology — Rexy-5097 ─────────────────────────────────
# The deterministic spine. Every published number is produced here, so changes
# carry methodology meaning and need the statistical owner.
/statistics/                    @Rexy-5097
/experiments/                   @Rexy-5097
/docs/methodology/              @Rexy-5097
# The determinism boundary itself (dossier section 05). Weakening this test
# silently removes the reproducibility guarantee, so it is owner-gated.
/tests/test_architecture.py     @Rexy-5097

# ─── Ingestion, compliance and sources — slazyverse ─────────────────────────
/ingestion/                     @slazyverse
/compliance/                    @slazyverse
/source_registry/               @slazyverse

# ─── Product surface — Basant-creator ───────────────────────────────────────
/api/                           @Basant-creator
/dashboard/                     @Basant-creator

# ─── Cross-domain contracts — joint ownership ───────────────────────────────
# Canonical schemas are the contract between collection and computation.
# Both domain owners review, because a schema change breaks one side or the other.
/schemas/                       @Rexy-5097 @slazyverse

# ─── Analytics and AI — Layer 3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reads the index, never writes it. Owned by the statistical owner because the
# layer boundary is a statistical guarantee, not a product decision.
/analytics/                     @Rexy-5097
/ai/                            @Rexy-5097

# ─── Repository, framework and CI governance — Rexy-5097 ────────────────────
/.github/                       @Rexy-5097
/docs/engineering/              @Rexy-5097
/docs/agentos/                  @Rexy-5097
/AGENTS.md                      @Rexy-5097
/CLAUDE.md                      @Rexy-5097
